## Voice

- OpenAI `gpt-4o-mini-tts`, voice **coral**. British English, contemporary Southern, warm/professional. No American pronunciation or vocabulary.
- Say **adviser**, not advisor. Say **Agreement in Principle** in full, never “AIP”.
- Say **Mortgage Easy** in VO (two words). On-screen brand is **MortgageEasy**.
- Do not stretch with `atempo`. Lock picture to transcribed speech, then still-frame QC at named times.
- Do not burn captions into the MP4. Site captions are HTML/VTT, shown only while muted.

## Picture

- Native speed only. Never freeze or slow-mo (`setpts` looked frozen). Do not loop talking-head clips.
- Do not dissolve two similar over-the-shoulder laptop shots — that ghosts. Change **camera angle**, or keep the same frame and change only the screen.
- Runway often washes laptop screens white. Prefer a held still of a known-good login frame, or overlay UI. Do not trust a “login” filename.
- **Family lock:** husband = olive-brown skin, short dark curls, olive shirt over white tee, no blazer. Wife = cream knit, shoulder-length brown hair. Two children in family scenes. Adviser (when used) = ~50, greying, navy blazer, light blue shirt.
- MortgageEasy **white tablet badge** top-left on branded live shots and graphic cards. No ME branding on generic property websites.
- Final export must be QuickTime/Safari-safe: Constrained Baseline, no B-frames, `setpts=N/24/TB`, stereo AAC, `+faststart`. Sparse High-profile keyframes caused the remortgage player to jump to the end.

## ffmpeg (this machine)

- Old binary: no `xfade`. Dissolves via trim + alpha overlay + concat.
- `ffmpeg -i` exits 1; duration parsing must not use `set -o pipefail` blindly.
- `apad` is flaky. Write decimals as `0.7`, not `.7`. Do not use `-shortest` if it truncates the logo/end.

## Site player

- Muted autoplay on scroll into view. Captions along the bottom while muted; hide them when unmuted.
- End card: **Start your journey** → `#your-journey`.
- Later products: reuse this player pattern (`[data-ftb-player]`) and these production rules; start from a duplicate of the last approved draft.
